# Data Quality Assessment

## 1. Project Overview

This document evaluates the quality of the Online Retail dataset before conducting business analysis.

## 2. Dataset Information

- Dataset Name: Online Retail Dataset
- Source: UCI Machine Learning Repository
- File Format: Excel (.xlsx)
- Business Domain: E-commerce / Retail

## 3. Data Quality Checks
### 3.1Duplicate Records Assessment

The dataset was examined using Microsoft Excel's Remove Duplicates feature.

All eight columns were selected to identify completely identical records.

**Results:**

| Description | Record Count |
|---|---:|
| Original records | 541,909 |
| Duplicate records identified | 5,267 |
| Unique records remaining | 536,642 |

**Key Finding:**

A total of 5,267 duplicate rows were identified based on matching values across all eight columns.

**Business Impact:**

Duplicate records may lead to inaccurate sales calculations and misleading business performance reports.

**Recommendation:**

Investigate duplicate transactions and remove confirmed duplicate records from the analytical working dataset while preserving the original source data.

The following checks will be performed:

1. Missing values
2. Duplicate records
3. Negative quantities
4. Zero unit prices
5. Negative unit prices
6. Incorrect data formats

## 4. Data Quality Findings

### 4.1 Missing Values Assessment

The dataset was examined to identify missing values in important columns.

| Column | Missing Records |
|---|---:|
| CustomerID | 135,080 |
| Description | 1,454 |

Key Findings

1. CustomerID: A significant number of transaction records do not contain customer identification information. 
2. Description: Some transaction records have missing product descriptions, which may affect product identification and product-level analysis.

**Business Impact:**

Missing customer information may limit the ability to understand individual customer purchasing behaviour.
Missing product descriptions may create challenges when analysing product performance.

**Recommendation:**

Investigate missing records before conducting customer and product-level analysis. Avoid deleting records without understanding their business context.

